# SATUSEHAT-2 — Sandbox API Adapter & FHIR Submission

Builds on the SATUSEHAT-1 readiness foundation. The adapter is real but stays
**OFF by default** and **sandbox-only**; production SATUSEHAT is fail-closed.

1. Production SATUSEHAT stays disabled in SATUSEHAT-2. `satusehat.sandbox_only`
   defaults true; the gateway/host guard reject any non-sandbox environment/host.
2. Only sandbox hostnames on `config('satusehat.allowed_hosts.sandbox')` are
   reachable. `SatusehatHostGuard::assertAllowedBaseUrl()` runs before every
   outbound call (token + FHIR). HTTPS only; embedded credentials rejected;
   `withoutRedirecting()` prevents redirect host escape.
3. TLS verification is NEVER disabled (`Http::withoutVerifying()` is banned in
   runtime, deploy, and evidence).
4. Secrets/tokens are never logged, never put in an exception message, never
   stored in the DB, never returned by `status()`/`connectionStatus()`, never in
   audit/OperationOutcome. The token cache key uses a non-reversible fingerprint.
5. The OAuth token comes only from `client_credentials`; it is cached
   (Illuminate cache, not the DB), refreshed a buffer before expiry, and acquired
   under a distributed lock so concurrent workers request at most one token.
6. No auto-send. No scheduler selects/sends candidates. No send at payment /
   visit-completed / RME-finalized. No "Send All"; no default selection. The
   operator must explicitly review, approve, and queue a batch, and hold
   `send_satusehat_submissions`.
7. `SatusehatSubmissionService::queue()` is fail-closed: it refuses while the
   gateway is not enabled (kill switch `send_enabled=false`). The driver job is
   dispatched only AFTER the transaction commits.
8. Every state change goes through `SatusehatSubmissionStateMachine` +
   `SatusehatSubmissionProcessingService`. Free-form status writes from a
   controller/Blade are forbidden. Transitions are locked, transactional, and
   audited.
9. The source hash is re-verified before each outbound request. Clinical drift
   after preparation aborts the submission (`source_drift_aborted`) — never send
   stale/fabricated data.
10. Idempotency: a successfully-sent (succeeded/reconciled) resource is never
    resent; `trx_satusehat_submission_items.idempotency_key` is UNIQUE at the DB
    level; the claim step no-ops on a terminal item.
11. An ambiguous outcome (timeout/reset after the body may have been sent, or a
    500) is `unknown_outcome` → reconciliation via GET-by-id, NEVER a blind
    re-POST. No remote id → stays `reconciliation_required` for operator review.
12. Retry is classified + bounded: 401 → evict token + retry once then permanent;
    429 → honor `Retry-After`; 502/503/504 → retryable; 400/403/409/422 →
    permanent. The circuit breaker opens after repeated hard failures.
13. NIK/KTP never appears in a URL, log, audit, OperationOutcome, or payload.
    Identifier verification GETs by IHS id (never a NIK query). Odontogram,
    handwriting, scans, attachments are never sent (asserted by
    `SatusehatFhirValidator`).
14. Terminology is never invented. Procedure/Condition codes come only from an
    active versioned `SatusehatCodeMapping`; an unmapped treatment stays blocked.
    There is no structured diagnosis source, so Condition is not emitted.
15. Branch isolation: queue/batch actions are scoped to the actor's RME branches
    server-side (`BranchService::rmeEnabledIds()`); the request `branch_id` is
    never trusted.
16. No external HTTP call is made while a DB transaction is open (claim →
    network-outside-tx → record).
17. A clinical/billing transaction is never rolled back by a SATUSEHAT failure.
18. Live sandbox verification uses ONLY synthetic/test identifiers via
    `php artisan satusehat:sandbox-verify --live --confirm-sandbox` (refuses
    production; requires explicit confirmation; never prints secret/NIK/payload;
    never runs during deploy). Mock-only success is NOT a GO.
19. Production activation is a separate, explicitly-approved sprint. Until then
    production host is fail-closed and `SATUSEHAT_ENABLED`/`SATUSEHAT_SEND_ENABLED`
    stay false on the VPS.
